# A maintainer's personal agent skills (installed with `npx skills`) and their
# lockfile. They're tooling for one person's workflow, not part of the app or
# of what self-hosters and contributors need, so they stay on disk untracked.
.agents/
skills-lock.json

# Claude Code's per-machine files. The desktop app runs parallel sessions in git
# worktrees under .claude/worktrees/, inside this folder, and each one is a full
# checkout of the repo. Left unignored, they show up in `git status`, and
# Prettier (format:check) and oxlint (lint) read .gitignore, so every worktree's
# copy of the code gets checked as well. Vitest doesn't read this file, so
# vite.config.ts excludes the folder from the unit tests separately.
# settings.local.json holds personal permissions. Only these two are ignored,
# so a team-wide .claude/settings.json could still be committed later.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json
